# Tina live preview fields

Visitor-visible content is rendered twice: the public page (from `astro:content`) and the Tina island in `src/components/islands/` (live edit). A field only shows in the admin preview, and only focuses its form input on click, when the island renders it with `tinaField`.

When you add or change a field that visitors see:

1. Add it to the Tina collection in `tina/config.ts` and the Astro schema in `src/content.config.ts`.
2. Render it on the public page.
3. Render the same value in the matching island, with `tinaField(data, 'fieldName')` on the element that shows the value. Hide it when empty.
4. Keep the label and order aligned with the public page.

Portfolio project details (location, client, date, project cost, size, architect, engineer, contractor) go through `ProjectSpecs`. Pass `fields` from `PortfolioBody` so each value stays click-to-edit.

Do not stop at the form. If the island does not render the field, editors will not see it update in the live preview.
